Come on, stop.

261
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:47,040
Please forgive me.

262
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:55,160
It's made it all the way to the
old King's Plateau. Damn it.

263
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:57,148
There's not much city left.

264
00:17:57,540 --> 00:18:00,617
People are going to start
dying one after another soon.

265
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:02,660
Keep pushing. This is it.

266
00:18:02,860 --> 00:18:04,820
Even a second could save lives.

267
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:09,940
Hey. I lost count.

268
00:18:10,180 --> 00:18:12,797
How much longer until
Lucy comes back? I...

269
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,020
I'm not sure.

270
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:19,000
The birdcage was halted for a moment,
but now it continues to close.

271
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:24,240
The time remaining is 60 seconds.

272
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:28,720
The time until Luffy
recovers is also 60 seconds.

273
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:38,177
We stopped it once, didn't we?

274
00:18:38,260 --> 00:18:40,520
We'll do it again if we have to.

275
00:18:44,580 --> 00:18:45,680
Get pushing!

276
00:18:46,300 --> 00:18:47,160
Let's go!

277
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:57,020
You gotta remember what's at stake here.

278
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:59,080
Either you push or you die.

279
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:01,800
You're not helping. Just shut up.

280
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,471
We all got too many dreams to give up now.

281
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:06,620
No way we're gonna die.

282
00:19:08,260 --> 00:19:09,090
Hooray!

283
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:24,440
Stacy, everybody, please.

284
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:27,140
We have all seen enough suffering.

285
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:34,851
Are you ready, everybody?

286
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:36,310
Huh?

287
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:37,330
Huh?

288
00:19:37,413 --> 00:19:39,480
It won't be much longer now!

289
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:41,820
Who's talking?

290
00:19:48,300 --> 00:19:50,260
Where's that coming from?

291
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:51,740
Some kind of PA?

292
00:19:52,340 --> 00:19:56,320
Our hero is on his way! Hey!

293
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:58,280
There he is!

294
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:04,580
That's Jax, isn't it?

295
00:20:04,760 --> 00:20:06,642
The announcer from the Coliseum?

296
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:08,780
What are you doing up there?

297
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:10,060
He's lost it.

298
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,600
Surely you remember him.

299
00:20:12,740 --> 00:20:14,975
Whatever this is, now is not the time.

300
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:19,677
The whole kingdom's about
to be destroyed, you know.

301
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,840
We'd rather hear from King Rick.

302
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:24,200
What that?

303
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:26,040
I need to remind you.

304
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:31,759
Unpredictable in nature and
irrepressible in spirit,

305
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:34,900
he burst onto the sea
and, more importantly,

306
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:36,700
into our hearts.

307
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:41,980
The hero who lit up the Coliseum
like a shining star! Shining star?

308
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:45,120
There's only one answer, surely.

309
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:47,000
He means me.

310
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:54,140
Hey, I know I said I'd
stay here with you, but...

311
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:58,480
Well, it turns out my fans need me. Sorry.

312
00:21:00,220 --> 00:21:03,000
Hello! Trafalgar! What? Where did he go?

313
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:06,777
His courage.

314
00:21:06,860 --> 00:21:09,040
Rocked my soul.

315
00:21:10,520 --> 00:21:15,237
He tamed the savage bull that struck
fear into the hearts of all gladiators.

316
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:19,197
His fearsome fists fell
the giant even the living

317
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:22,920
legend Don Chinchao
faltered before his might.

318
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:28,697
Though small in stature, his energy
was felt through all of the coliseum.

319
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:31,120
No, through all of Dressrosa!

320
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:34,160
A man who was born to be free,

321
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:38,361
who fought perfectly, who struck
a chord in our hearts brilliantly.

322
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:40,660
Now are you with me?

323
00:21:42,180 --> 00:21:44,960
Yeah, I saw him. That guy.

324
00:21:45,340 --> 00:21:46,940
He was pretty amazing.

325
00:21:47,340 --> 00:21:48,900
He blew me away, too.

326
00:21:49,140 --> 00:21:51,657
Everyone in the city
was watching him fight.

327
00:21:51,740 --> 00:21:53,280
You know his name?

328
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:56,030
Lucy!

329
00:21:57,900 --> 00:21:59,417
What are you getting at?

330
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:02,180
How is a gladiator
supposed to save us now?

331
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:06,630
Please...

332
00:22:06,713 --> 00:22:07,543
Lucy...

333
00:22:08,260 --> 00:22:09,500
Please... Help me...

334
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:11,748
But Lucy was only an alien!

335
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:13,190
That's right!

336
00:22:13,460 --> 00:22:16,300
He has another name you don't know!

337
00:22:17,340 --> 00:22:19,160
Would you like to hear it?

338
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:26,097
He's a pirate.

339
00:22:26,180 --> 00:22:28,317
Known as Straw Hat.

340
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:29,860
Monkey D.

341
00:22:30,260 --> 00:22:31,090
Lukey

342
00:22:32,260 --> 00:22:35,057
He sure had me fooled with that beard.

343
00:22:35,140 --> 00:22:37,337
I understand your reservations.

344
00:22:37,420 --> 00:22:40,337
You must be wary about
trusting another pirate.

345
00:22:40,420 --> 00:22:42,257
When Doflamingo has been lying.

346
00:22:42,340 --> 00:22:44,917
And grinding us under
his heel for so long.

347
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:45,857
However.

348
00:22:45,940 --> 00:22:48,717
He's different from
the Don Quixote family.

349
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:53,640
who tried to pass themselves off as our
saviors that night so many years ago.

350
00:22:54,140 --> 00:22:55,728
You don't have to trust me.

351
00:22:56,860 --> 00:23:01,660
Instead, listen to King Rick, who
placed his faith in Straw Hat Luffy.

352
00:23:05,180 --> 00:23:07,520
This is the call before the storm.

353
00:23:08,120 --> 00:23:11,477
Lucy is taking a breather right
now in preparation for round two,

354
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:14,120
but he's going to come back even stronger.

355
00:23:14,820 --> 00:23:18,400
So raise your hands in
celebration, Dressrosa.

356
00:23:20,260 --> 00:23:24,760
Because I spoke to Lucy,
and he made me a promise.

357
00:23:30,020 --> 00:23:32,420
He'll face Doflamingo!

358
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:43,600
And knock him out in one punch!

359
00:23:53,980 --> 00:23:56,057
He sure talks big.

360
00:23:56,140 --> 00:23:57,997
I'm making this quick, Captain.

361
00:23:58,080 --> 00:23:59,317
Because I'm slipping.

362
00:23:59,400 --> 00:24:00,880
Real fast.

363
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:05,320
I can't wait.

364
00:24:09,240 --> 00:24:11,437
Hey, Joe Flamingo.

365
00:24:11,520 --> 00:24:13,780
You hear that?

366
00:24:15,420 --> 00:24:16,457
You phony.

367
00:24:16,540 --> 00:24:18,297
Cheating our king.

368
00:24:18,380 --> 00:24:20,577
Filling our streets with lies.

369
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:22,957
Sitting on a misbegotten throne.

370
00:24:23,040 --> 00:24:24,957
Build on a mountain of injustice.

371
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:27,997
But now you must face your trial.

372
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:30,440
Your cruelty ends today.

373
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:36,790
Guts.

374
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:40,737
That's right, Doflamingo.

375
00:24:40,820 --> 00:24:43,157
I see straight through you.

376
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:45,677
If you're mad, come and get me!

377
00:24:45,760 --> 00:24:49,100
Keep your filthy hands
up, Viola and Rebecca.

378
00:24:51,180 --> 00:24:53,240
And soon enough,

379
00:24:53,740 --> 00:24:58,360
the Coliseum Shining Star,
our Lucy, will take the stage.

380
00:24:58,840 --> 00:25:02,860
Let's show him how we feel
and give the man a cheer.

381
00:25:12,660 --> 00:25:13,960
The Mr.

382
00:25:14,120 --> 00:25:16,100
Lupin, let's go!

383
00:25:28,580 --> 00:25:30,100
I wrote it!

384
00:25:33,080 --> 00:25:33,910
What's wrong?

385
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:36,657
It's like their injuries
came back all of a sudden.

386
00:25:36,740 --> 00:25:38,357
They're dropping like flies.

387
00:25:38,440 --> 00:25:39,911
Because time has run out.

388
00:25:40,560 --> 00:25:43,797
These people were the ones who
were given the dandelictures first,

389
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:45,277
and now they're wearing off.

390
00:25:45,360 --> 00:25:47,478
And they aren't going to work twice.

391
00:25:49,260 --> 00:25:50,180
I'm sorry.

392
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:52,017
That's the best thing to do.

393
00:25:52,100 --> 00:25:55,120
I tried, but my ability
just didn't come enough.

394
00:25:55,600 --> 00:25:57,480
I did such an awful thing.

395
00:25:57,800 --> 00:26:00,212
I gave them a host, and I yanked it away.

396
00:26:00,560 --> 00:26:02,740
That's not true, Princess Moncheree.

397
00:26:02,860 --> 00:26:04,317
If it wasn't for your help,

398
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:08,929
there's no telling just how many lives
the birdcage might have claimed today.

399
00:26:09,640 --> 00:26:10,700
Do you see?

400
00:26:11,660 --> 00:26:14,200
You made a miracle happen down there.

401
00:26:15,580 --> 00:26:16,780
Hey, come on!

402
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:17,820
Don't give up!

403
00:26:18,500 --> 00:26:22,057
Clear out the injured and have the
people in the back take their place.

404
00:26:22,140 --> 00:26:23,840
Bring in some fresh troops!

405
00:26:24,540 --> 00:26:25,370
Roger!

406
00:26:25,680 --> 00:26:31,220
We'll hold our ground at any cost until
Lucy gets rid of the birdcage for good!

407
00:26:33,900 --> 00:26:36,380
They were able to stall it long enough.

408
00:26:36,620 --> 00:26:39,796
Thanks to you, they'll survive
till Loopyland returns.

409
00:26:41,860 --> 00:26:43,680
It won't be long now.

410
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:46,746
Let's begin the countdown
to Lucy's countdown.

411
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:51,940
Call out his name.

412
00:26:52,160 --> 00:26:54,800
Make sure he can hear us.

413
00:27:03,460 --> 00:27:04,290
Lose it!

414
00:27:04,373 --> 00:27:05,203
Lose it!

415
00:27:05,286 --> 00:27:07,340
Count from three!

416
00:27:10,580 --> 00:27:11,617
Lose it!

417
00:27:11,700 --> 00:27:12,760
Lose it!

418
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:15,700
Lose it! Lose it! Two!

419
00:27:24,660 --> 00:27:25,977
Lose it!

420
00:27:26,060 --> 00:27:27,840
Lose it! One!

421
00:27:28,940 --> 00:27:30,300
What a joke.

422
00:27:32,580 --> 00:27:35,317
Your time is up, Doflamingo.

423
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:38,097
Lucy's gonna knock you out cold.

424
00:27:38,180 --> 00:27:40,240
One punch and you're toast.

425
00:28:01,760 --> 00:28:05,320
And now, you can go quiet, too.

426
00:28:07,440 --> 00:28:09,100
Forever, that is.

427
00:28:19,760 --> 00:28:22,460
I'm sorry, Biela! Wake up, Rebecca!

428
00:28:22,940 --> 00:28:24,120
Close your eyes!

429
00:28:24,400 --> 00:28:26,165
You don't have to see a thing.

430
00:28:26,420 --> 00:28:27,920
This is just a bad dream.

431
00:28:28,580 --> 00:28:31,580
Once it's over, you can
strike it from your memory.

432
00:28:32,060 --> 00:28:33,160
I'll forgive you.

433
00:28:33,400 --> 00:28:35,576
All that matters is that you move on.

434
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:37,560
Please be happy.

435
00:28:41,940 --> 00:28:42,980
Stop that!

436
00:28:44,440 --> 00:28:45,420
Don't be upset.

437
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:47,400
It's not your fault.

438
00:28:48,240 --> 00:28:50,517
I'm sorry I have to leave you like this.

439
00:28:50,600 --> 00:28:51,780
I know it will hurt.

440
00:28:52,020 --> 00:28:54,138
I know it won't be easy to overcome.

441
00:28:58,920 --> 00:28:59,750
No!

442
00:29:05,920 --> 00:29:06,750
No!

443
00:29:33,540 --> 00:29:35,320
Get back!

444
00:29:36,280 --> 00:29:38,960
Lucy is here at last!

445
00:29:40,760 --> 00:29:50,380
Lucy!

446
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:54,980
Lucy! Lucy!

447
00:29:58,980 --> 00:30:00,020
Star-Hat!

448
00:30:13,360 --> 00:30:16,040
This is all rather dramatic, isn't it?

449
00:30:16,280 --> 00:30:20,280
But still, I imagine it took a
lot just to recover your Haki.

450
00:30:22,460 --> 00:30:25,920
Why, it's probably a struggle
for you just to stand.

451
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:31,230
Maybe.

452
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:34,780
But you're no better off.

453
00:30:41,740 --> 00:30:42,570
Lucy!

454
00:30:49,100 --> 00:30:49,930
Samples.

455
00:30:54,880 --> 00:30:55,710
Rebecca!

456
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:08,402
That's where you crawled off to.

457
00:31:10,200 --> 00:31:11,030
Perfect.

458
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:13,160
You've got front row seats.

459
00:31:13,560 --> 00:31:17,200
Now watch as I crush the
only hope you've got left.

460
00:31:25,080 --> 00:31:27,480
Time forever, White!

461
00:31:31,980 --> 00:31:35,540
They turned the whole block into strings!

462
00:31:39,660 --> 00:31:40,490
Lucy!

463
00:31:42,440 --> 00:31:43,560
Damn you!

464
00:31:45,200 --> 00:31:47,200
It's no use.

465
00:31:50,780 --> 00:31:52,540
Thousand arrows!

466
00:31:54,280 --> 00:31:55,540
Flapping threat!

467
00:31:58,800 --> 00:32:00,680
Now die!

468
00:32:02,460 --> 00:32:03,540
Over me!

469
00:32:21,140 --> 00:32:22,520
Done already.

470
00:32:22,960 --> 00:32:24,725
What about your comeback, huh?

471
00:32:29,960 --> 00:32:34,020
I'm not seeing that miraculous
Haki of yours, Lucy.

472
00:32:37,580 --> 00:32:39,820
Is he gonna be okay?

473
00:33:12,600 --> 00:33:15,580
That didn't look good Did Lucy win?

474
00:33:15,800 --> 00:33:16,660
I can't tell.

475
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:20,077
The birdcage is still here.

476
00:33:20,160 --> 00:33:22,380
Lucy, hurry!

477
00:33:28,140 --> 00:33:29,540
What the hell?

478
00:33:30,120 --> 00:33:33,060
My body's moving on its own.

479
00:33:36,540 --> 00:33:39,480
I can't believe you
survived that last assault.

480
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:42,257
I'll have to inhale
you properly next time.

481
00:33:42,340 --> 00:33:46,105
Or maybe I should force you to
kill all of your friends instead.

482
00:33:46,480 --> 00:33:50,680
Ha, ha, ha, came running back
with your tail between your legs.

483
00:33:51,380 --> 00:33:54,360
Well, you escaped death
again. That's good.

484
00:33:54,920 --> 00:33:56,540
Next time, I'm gonna win!

485
00:33:57,600 --> 00:34:00,280
Your famous Kong gun didn't do the trick.

486
00:34:00,440 --> 00:34:02,160
This guy was huge!

487
00:34:02,400 --> 00:34:05,677
Way bigger than the last one,
so the move didn't work, really!

488
00:34:05,760 --> 00:34:06,940
It wasn't fair!

489
00:34:07,840 --> 00:34:08,817
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

490
00:34:08,900 --> 00:34:11,018
Sounds like you're in trouble, then.

491
00:34:14,100 --> 00:34:16,394
Oh, well, if the kong gun doesn't work,

492
00:34:16,540 --> 00:34:19,658
then you'll just have to
come up with something else.

493
00:34:20,060 --> 00:34:21,820
I guess, but what?

494
00:34:24,120 --> 00:34:25,460
It's almost tragic.

495
00:34:26,800 --> 00:34:31,097
All those little insects were so much
better off dancing on their streams,

496
00:34:31,180 --> 00:34:33,768
trapped in my cage as
they were meant to be.

497
00:34:36,800 --> 00:34:37,630
Insects?

498
00:34:37,713 --> 00:34:39,020
That's what you think?

499
00:34:41,260 --> 00:34:42,090
Of course.

500
00:34:42,173 --> 00:34:43,704
Humans are nothing but garbage.

501
00:34:44,140 --> 00:34:46,740
That's enough already!

502
00:35:01,240 --> 00:35:02,420
We're waiting, Lupi!

503
00:35:12,160 --> 00:35:13,340
Hmph. Go ahead.

504
00:35:17,260 --> 00:35:19,680
Turn into your stupid balloon man, Finn.

505
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:21,680
That'll be more fun for me.

506
00:35:21,940 --> 00:35:23,817
I'll have you kill all your friends,

507
00:35:23,900 --> 00:35:27,312
then kill everyone else in the
kingdom while you're at it.

508
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:44,400
Alright, fourth gear!

509
00:35:48,980 --> 00:35:50,120
He cut them.

510
00:35:57,620 --> 00:36:00,060
You can't have much strength remaining.

511
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:03,165
How long do you think
you can last in that war?

512
00:36:07,880 --> 00:36:08,960
This is it!

513
00:36:12,780 --> 00:36:15,817
Sure you want to challenge
someone like me in the air?

514
00:36:15,900 --> 00:36:17,180
You got some nerve.

515
00:36:20,400 --> 00:36:22,260
Still beating me in one hit?

516
00:36:22,620 --> 00:36:24,080
Let's see it then.

517
00:36:38,260 --> 00:36:40,837
I don't know if I like
you looking down on me.

518
00:36:40,920 --> 00:36:41,917
Well, no matter.

519
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:46,118
I'll just have to drag you to the
ground and make you my puppet again.

520
00:36:46,660 --> 00:36:47,617
Every time.

521
00:36:47,700 --> 00:36:51,340
You just grab whatever
you want and strangle it!

522
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:57,840
You can't have everything!

523
00:36:58,200 --> 00:37:00,520
You can't control everyone either!

524
00:37:10,560 --> 00:37:14,300
Seeing you makes it hard to even breathe!

525
00:37:14,960 --> 00:37:16,320
That's not my fault.

526
00:37:16,580 --> 00:37:17,720
Blame your fate.

527
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:21,059
To be born as a human is
to be born as living trash.

528
00:37:21,540 --> 00:37:24,920
It's my divine right to
control you as I please.

529
00:37:25,340 --> 00:37:26,840
I'm gonna kick your ass.

530
00:37:27,380 --> 00:37:29,440
Then everyone here will be free.

531
00:37:29,640 --> 00:37:31,581
